ts plus leftovers, and when space runs out, product 1 is the one lost. So the best level is roughly 1.1–1.2× the forecast.\n- **Fixed order cost.** Candidate 5 places 26 orders instead of 13, which adds about 468 in order fees. That is more than daily ordering saves by smoothing out randomness.\n- **Candidate 2.** Ordering every 3 days saves about 144 in order fees. But it has the least safety stock, the most variance per delivery, and deliveries of up to 150 units that risk overflowing.\n\n**Conclusion.** The most likely top four are 6, 0, 3 and 7. Candidate 4 (too much stock) and candidate 2 are borderline, and candidates 1 and 5 are the most likely to be in the bottom half."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4434, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4434}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:39:30.275Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSM8njArctjTuVtFWnA"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014s5dKxFiwVZJoADvz2FLGk", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVSM94baAWanfgWb9Wmy", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014s5dKxFiwVZJoADvz2FLGk", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.7, 0.2, 0.3, 0.65, 0.35, 0.15, 0.75, 0.6]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_s