and that is correct there: a shortage costs 11 against 5 for a surplus.\n- **1 — bottom half.** It orders exactly the forecast, below the true average demand. With stock usually near zero, I estimate about 140 units short across both products, costing about 1,800.\n- **4 — bottom half.** At 1.3×, surplus write-offs come to roughly 2,000. Arrivals plus stock carried over can also exceed the 164-unit warehouse, and that overflow is paid for but lost.\n- **5 — bottom half.** It orders daily, which is 26 fees of 36, or about 470 more than ordering every two days. Daily orders gain little, since leftovers carry over anyway.\n- **2 — borderline, leaning bottom.** It orders every three days at about 1.05×, which saves around 180 in fees. But its large deliveries plus carried-over stock can exceed warehouse capacity, and its margin above average demand is thin.\n\nThe probabilities below reflect these estimates."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4431, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4431}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:39:53.111Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSMuxLdWosEpCYo69NA"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01669cGsyLo6FKX98qjZEsaS", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVSMvCE7UqpmfqxWzT5L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content":